<urn:atm:triage:finding/BA4-QA2-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BA4-QA2-001" ;
  triage:title "cli_surface_baseline.json was not regenerated for BA.4's intentional CLI-surface changes; cli_surface_matches_committed_baseline fails deterministically" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA-2 (converged: req-qa, arch-qa, ruthless-boundary-qa, rust-qa-agent, plus quality-mgr's own independent reproduction -- 5 of 6 dispatched reviewers plus quality-mgr), PR #1408 @ 85da7db99, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1408#issuecomment-5643235732. crates/atm/tests/cli_surface_baseline.json was not regenerated for this sprint's intentional CLI-surface changes. cargo test -p agent-team-mail --features cli-surface-dump --test cli_surface's cli_surface_matches_committed_baseline fails deterministically: atm list 'member'/'task_events'/'tasks' arguments removed or renamed; atm queue/send 'task_complete' num_args changed {max:1,min:1}->{max:0,min:0} and has_default false->true; no top-level 'task' subcommand entry at all despite atm task (5 subcommands) being new surface added by this sprint. Not flaky -- fully deterministic, root-caused, reproduced independently by quality-mgr (local, fresh CARGO_TARGET_DIR), ruthless-boundary-qa, arch-qa, req-qa, and rust-qa-agent. Confirmed live on CI identically on ubuntu-latest and macos-latest (run https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/actions/runs/34669585703). Expected fallout of the sprint's own 'Paths to delete' work; the change itself is correct and intentional, only the checked-in baseline snapshot was never regenerated. fenix's ruling (https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1408#issuecomment-5643246196): STANDS. Reproduced at 85da7db99 with the same seven breaking entries plus the missing task subcommand tree. Regenerate the baseline with the gen_cli_docs example (also refreshes the version-suffixed CLI reference), commit, re-run clean. Routed to solar (not cipher) because feature/ba4-atm-task-commands is solar's single-writer worktree and a second writer on a live branch breaks the single-writer rule; folded into BA4-FIX-R2-1789184679." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ba" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "ci-gate" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "crates/atm/tests/cli_surface_baseline.json, crates/atm/tests/cli_surface.rs" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T03:50:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:devFixNote "dev-fixed at b84a46a1e (BA4-FIX-R2, fenix-verified from the dev side)." ;
  triage:closedBy "fenix" ;
  triage:resolutionNote "marked fixed at b84a46a1e per fenix's explicit instruction (ATM 2026-09-12T04:39:18Z): QA verifies on docs/ba6-task-nudge-documentation (BA.6 = BA.4 b84a46a1e + merge BA.5 7997f8aaa), not via a separate BA4-QA3 delta pass -- feature/ba4-atm-task-commands is now frozen." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BA4 ;
